          "quote": "(node (ref \"U10\") (pin \"14\") (pinfunction \"LAN_PORT3_TX-\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Shorts the Ethernet transmit pair to ground, preventing Ethernet operation and potentially damaging the module.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C5"],
      "pins": ["C5.1", "C5.2"],
      "nets": ["Net-(U5-A)", "Net-(Q2-D)"],
      "observed": "C5 is specified as 4.7uF/25V in the netlist.",
      "expected": "The specification states C5 should be 1uF/25V (part of the EPD driver's G1-group capacitor set).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C5\") (value \"4.7uF/25V\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Changes the EPD boost/charge-pump capacitance, potentially affecting display power sequencing or performance.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain several anomalies: C12 is an unconnected capacitor with an inductor footprint, U10 Ethernet pins 13/14 are shorted to ground, and C5 has a wrong value."
